# Cloudflare Pages security headers
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Notes (2026-05-19):
# - HSTS: 6-month max-age, NO preload, NO includeSubDomains yet.
#   Per Sally's review: preload is hard to roll back (browser-baked list),
#   and includeSubDomains can break any *.michaelreflects.com subdomain
#   that isn't HTTPS-only. Revisit both after 6+ months of stable HSTS.
# - X-Frame-Options: DENY (no one needs to embed this in a frame).
# - Permissions-Policy: deny features the site never uses, including the
#   privacy-hostile FLoC interest-cohort.
# - CSP (JOURNAL-CSP-01 Phase 2b): the enforcing Content-Security-Policy must equal
#   csp/phase2.policy, the Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only (the stricter Phase 3
#   measurement: no 'unsafe-inline' in script-src) must equal
#   csp/phase3-report-only.policy, and Reporting-Endpoints names the collector
#   (functions/api/csp-report.js). The Pages build (tools/pages-build.sh,
#   CSP_PHASE=2b-enforce) fails if any of the three differs. Edit them together.
#   Why each host is allowed: docs/csp/phase2a-report-only.md.
#   Pages Functions (reply pages, weather.json, deleted posts, the collector) are not
#   covered by this file and set their own headers.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
